I have a javascript file that sends a json object to the server for processing with an R script. I can get this to work fine with smaller datasets (i.e smaller json objects) but when I send a longer json object to the server, it is not recognizing the object as valid json.<br><br>Is there a maximum length for json objects when using Rapache or RJSONIO?<br><br>Please let meknow if anyone has experienced enything similar or has any thoughts.<br><br>Thanks,<br><br>Andrew<br><br>Here is a sample from my R script:<br><br># supposedly loads all installed packages...<br>lapply(.packages(all.available = TRUE), function(xx) library(xx,     character.only = TRUE)) <br><br>binpost  &lt;- receiveBin()<br>postdata &lt;- rawToChar(binpost)<br><br> if (isValidJSON(postdata, TRUE)) {<br><br>   v &lt;- &quot;looks like valid json&quot;<br>    <br> } else {<br><br>    v &lt;- &quot;looks NOT like valid json&quot;<br>    <br>    resdata &lt;- toJSON(v)<br>    cat(resdata)<br> }<br><br>... and the javascript (where &#39;formdata&#39; should be valid json)<br><br>$.ajax({
<br>            type: &quot;POST&quot;,
<br>            url: &quot;<a href="http://localhost/povApp/rscripts/regression.r" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://localhost/povApp/rscripts/regression.r&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793239580755000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1dShYHNqFuW37OTdRQQNx8">http://localhost/povApp/rscripts/regression.r</a>&quot;,
<br>            data: formdata,
<br>            contentType: &quot;application/json&quot; 
<br>         });
<br> <br>         $(&quot;#result&quot;).ajaxSuccess(function(event, xhr, settings) {
<br>            $(this).text(&#39;IT WORKS!!!&#39; + xhr.responseText );
<br>            console.log(xhr.responseText);
<br>         });
<br>         $(&quot;#result&quot;).ajaxError(function(event, xhr, settings) {
<br>            $(this).text(&quot;Request failed&quot;);
<br>         });<br>
